/*!
    \page qt-tools-utilities.html
    \title Tools and utilities
    \brief Lists development tools for the Qt Framework, grouped by their
           primary function.

    Qt provides a comprehensive set of command-line and graphical development
    tools covering the full development workflow: configuring builds,
    preprocessing assets, generating boilerplate from interface descriptions
    (Protobuf, gRPC, D-Bus, SCXML, OPC UA, Remote Objects), running and
    analyzing QML code, managing translations, deploying to target platforms,
    and importing 3D assets.

    The tools listed on this page are included in the Qt Framework and
    installed with Qt. For the broader Qt ecosystem, including
    \l{\QC Documentation}{\QC},
    IDE extensions, AI tooling, QA tools, and commercial add-ons, see
    \l{https://www.qt.io/development/tools}{Qt development tools} and
    \l{https://www.qt.io/quality-assurance}{Qt QA software tools} on qt.io.

    For guidance on running these tools safely on projects whose origin you
    don't trust, see \l{Using Qt's Developer Tools Securely}.

    \section1 Build system

    Tools that drive Qt's build configuration and project file generation.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{qmake Manual}{qmake}
        \li Qt's traditional build system. Generates platform-specific Makefiles
            from \c{.pro} project files.
    \row
        \li \l{qt-cmake}
        \li Qt's primary build system is CMake. qt-cmake is a CMake wrapper that
            locates the Qt installation automatically, eliminating the need to
            set \c{CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH} when configuring Qt projects.
    \endtable

    \section1 Code generators

    Tools that generate C++ source from class declarations, or from interface
    and protocol description files.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Using the Meta-Object Compiler (moc)}{Meta-Object Compiler (moc)}
        \li Processes C++ class declarations that use Qt macros and generates
            the introspection code that powers signals and slots, dynamic
            properties, and runtime type information.
    \row
        \li \l{Qt D-Bus XML compiler (qdbusxml2cpp)}
        \li Generates C++ proxy and adaptor classes from a D-Bus introspection
            XML description.
    \row
        \li \l{Using the Qt SCXML Compiler (qscxmlc)}{Qt SCXML Compiler (qscxmlc)}
        \li Compiles SCXML state machine descriptions into C++ classes that
            integrate directly into a Qt application.
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Remote Objects Compiler}{Qt Remote Objects Compiler (repc)}
        \li Generates source and replica C++ classes from \c{.rep} interface
            files for use with \l{Qt Remote Objects}.
    \row
        \li \l{The Qt OPC UA data type generator}{Qt OPC UA data type generator (qopcuaxmldatatypes2cpp)}
        \li Generates C++ data type code from OPC UA NodeSet2 XML files for
            use with \l{Qt OPC UA}.
    \row
        \li \l{The qtgrpcgen Tool}{qtgrpcgen}
        \li Generates Qt-compatible gRPC client and server stub C++ classes from
            \c{.proto} files.
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Jenny: Java Code Generator}
        \li Generates C++ wrapper classes for Java APIs, enabling Qt APIs
            to be called from Java or Kotlin on Android.
    \row
        \li \l{User Interface Compiler (uic)}
        \li Converts \c{.ui} form files created in Qt Designer into C++ header
            files.
    \endtable

    \section1 Asset conditioning

    Tools that preprocess and convert source assets into forms consumed by the
    build or runtime: UI forms, binary resources, shaders, scalable vector
    graphics, distance field atlases, and animation files.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Resource Compiler (rcc)}
        \li Embeds application resources such as images, QML files, and
            translation files, into the application binary or as standalone
            \c{.rcc} files.
    \row
        \li \l{svgtoqml}
        \li Converts SVG files to QML components using Qt Quick Shapes, enabling
            scalable vector graphics without a raster image dependency.
    \row
        \li \l{QSB Manual}{Qt Shader Baker (qsb)}
        \li Compiles GLSL shaders into a multi-target package format (\c{.qsb})
            consumable by Qt's graphics stack across Vulkan, Metal, Direct3D,
            and OpenGL backends.
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Distance Field Generator Manual}{Qt Distance Field Generator}
        \li Pre-generates distance field texture atlases for text rendering,
            reducing startup time on resource-constrained embedded targets.
    \row
        \li \l{lottietoqml}
        \li Converts Lottie JSON animation files (as exported from Adobe After
            Effects and compatible tools) to QML components using
            \l{Qt Lottie Animation}.
    \endtable

    \section1 QML compilation

    Tools for compiling QML and JavaScript files to bytecode or native C++
    ahead of time, reducing startup cost at runtime.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{QML script compiler}
        \li Compiles functions and expressions in QML and JavaScript files to a
            byte code that can be interpreted or Just-in-time compiled by the
            QML engine.
    \row
        \li \l{QML type compiler}
        \li Translates QML types into C++ types that are ahead-of-time compiled
            as part of the user code.
    \endtable

    \section1 Formatters and linters

    Tools for analyzing and formatting QML source files.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{qmllint}
        \li Static analyzer for QML files. Detects binding errors, deprecated
            API usage, and other common mistakes at development time.
    \row
        \li \l{qmlformat}
        \li Formats QML files in accordance with the \l{QML Coding Conventions}.
    \row
        \li \l{QML Language Server}
        \li An LSP-compatible language server providing code completion,
            go-to-definition, and live diagnostics in any editor that supports
            the Language Server Protocol.
    \row
        \li \l{qmlcontextpropertydump}
        \li Scans a C++ source folder for potential context property definitions,
            and stores them in a format readable by \l{qmllint} and
            \l{QML Language Server}.
    \endtable

    \section1 3D assets

    Tools for importing and converting 3D content, and pre-processing physics
    collision data at build time.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Balsam Asset Import Tool}
        \li Imports 3D assets in formats such as FBX, glTF 2, and OBJ and
            converts them to Qt Quick 3D's native format.
    \row
        \li \l{Balsam Asset Import Tool#balsam-ui}{Balsam UI}
        \li A graphical front end for the Balsam tool.
    \row
        \li \l{Cooker tool}{Cooker}
        \li Pre-processes and bakes collision meshes for
            \l {Qt Quick 3D Physics} at build time, avoiding runtime cost on
            target devices.
    \row
        \li \l{The Material Editor tool}{Material Editor (materialeditor)}
        \li A GUI tool for authoring \l{CustomMaterial}{CustomMaterials}
            for \l{Qt Quick 3D}.
    \row
        \li \l{Instancer Tool}{Instancer}
        \li Converts \l{Qt Quick 3D} instancing tables from \l{FileInstancing}
            XML to a binary format for direct memory mapping at runtime.
    \endtable

    \section1 Translation and localization

    Tools for extracting, converting, and compiling translation files.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Linguist Manual}{Qt Linguist}
        \li Qt's translation environment. Provides translators with a
            workflow for reviewing source strings, entering translations, and
            validating \c{.ts} files before release.
    \endtable

    The following tools are part of Qt Linguist.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Using lupdate}{lupdate}
        \li Extracts translatable strings from C++ and QML source files and
            creates or updates \c{.ts} translation files.
    \row
        \li \l{Using lupdate-pro}{lupdate-pro}
        \li Variant of \c{lupdate} that reads \c{.pro} project files to locate
            source files.
    \row
        \li \l{Using lrelease}{lrelease}
        \li Compiles \c{.ts} translation files into binary \c{.qm} format for
            use at runtime.
    \row
        \li \l{Using lrelease-pro}{lrelease-pro}
        \li Variant of \c{lrelease} that reads \c{.pro} project files.
    \row
        \li \l{Using lconvert}{lconvert}
        \li Converts between translation file formats (TS, XLIFF, PO, and
            others).
    \row
        \li \l{Using ltext2id}{ltext2id}
        \li Converts text-based translation files to ID-based format.
    \row
        \li \l{Using lcheck}{lcheck}
        \li Validates \c{.ts} files and reports common errors. Suitable for use
            in CI pipelines.
    \endtable

    \section1 Testing and diagnostics

    Tools for testing Qt applications, inspecting D-Bus services, and
    diagnosing runtime issues. For automated GUI and system-level testing,
    see \l{Squish GUI Test Automation Tool}{Squish}.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Qt D-Bus Viewer}
        \li A graphical browser for D-Bus services. Inspect objects, interfaces,
            and properties, and call methods interactively.
    \row
        \li \l{qmlpreview}
        \li Hot-reloads QML files on a connected device or host as they are
            saved, without restarting the application.
    \row
        \li \l{The androidtestrunner Tool}{androidtestrunner}
        \li Runs Qt auto-tests on Android devices or emulators and collects
            the results.
    \row
        \li \l{The qml utility}
        \li Loads and runs QML files without a compiled application wrapper.
            Useful for rapid prototyping and testing individual QML components.
    \endtable

    \section1 Profiling and tracing

    Tools for collecting and analyzing runtime performance data from Qt and
    QML applications.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{qmlprofiler}
        \li Retrieves QML tracing data from an application. The collected data
            can then be visualized in Qt Creator.
    \endtable

    \section1 Deployment tools

    Tools for packaging Qt applications for distribution to target platforms.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{The androiddeployqt Tool}
        \li Assembles a deployable Android APK or AAB from a compiled Qt
            application, bundling the required Qt libraries and assets.
    \row
        \li \l{The harmonydeployqt Tool}
        \li Assembles a deployable HarmonyOS Ability Package (HAP) from a
            compiled Qt application, bundling the required Qt libraries, plugins,
            and QML modules.
    \row
        \li \l{The macOS Deployment Tool}
        \li Automates the process of creating a deployable application bundle
            that contains Qt libraries as private frameworks.
    \row
        \li \l{The Windows Deployment Tool}
        \li Collects all required Qt libraries, plugins, QML
            modules, and runtime dependencies into a ready-to-run deployment
            folder.
    \endtable

    \section1 Qt Application Manager

    Qt Application Manager is the framework for building embedded System UIs
    that manage, sandbox, and control the lifecycle of applications.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Application Manager}
        \li The main application manager tool. Acts as a compositing window
            manager and application lifecycle controller for embedded System
            UIs.
    \endtable

    The following command-line utilities are part of the Qt Application Manager
    suite.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Controller (appman)}
        \li Remote-controls a running appman instance: start and stop
            applications, install packages, and query runtime state.
    \row
        \li \l{Packager (appman)}
        \li Creates, signs, and verifies application packages for installation
            by the application manager.
    \row
        \li \l{Package-Server (appman)}
        \li A lightweight development HTTP server that distributes application
            packages for over-the-air installation testing.
    \endtable

    \section1 ActiveQt, Windows COM integration

    Tools for working with COM and ActiveX on Windows: generating C++ bindings
    from type libraries, producing documentation, and testing ActiveX controls.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{The dumpcpp Tool (ActiveQt)}{dumpcpp}
        \li Generates C++ namespace and class definitions from a Windows COM
            type library, allowing Qt/C++ code to drive COM servers.
    \row
        \li \l{The dumpdoc Tool (ActiveQt)}{dumpdoc}
        \li Generates HTML documentation for a COM object from its type library.
    \row
        \li \l{IDC - The Interface Description Compiler (ActiveQt)}
               {Interface Description Compiler (idc)}
        \li Post-processes Qt plugin DLLs to register them as COM servers and
            generate the necessary IDL and type library metadata.
    \row
        \li \l{testcon - An ActiveX Test Container (ActiveQt)}
               {ActiveX Test Container (testcon)}
        \li An interactive container for testing and exploring ActiveX controls.
    \endtable

    \section1 UI design

    Tools for designing visual effects and application forms.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Quick Effect Maker}
        \li A visual node-based tool for designing and previewing custom
            fragment shader effects for Qt Quick items.
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Widgets Designer Manual}{Qt Widgets Designer}
        \li A WYSIWYG form and widget designer for Qt Widgets applications,
            producing \c{.ui} files consumed by \c{uic}.
    \endtable

    \section1 Documentation tools

    Tools for generating and browsing Qt documentation.

    \table
    \header
        \li Tool
        \li Description
    \row
        \li \l{QDoc Manual}{QDoc}
        \li Qt's documentation generator. Reads annotated C++ source and
            \c{.qdocconf} configuration files to produce HTML or Qt Help output.
    \row
        \li \l{Qt Assistant Manual}{Qt Assistant}
        \li Qt's offline documentation browser. Embeds in applications
            to provide context-sensitive help.
    \row
        \li \l{Generating Qt Help}{qhelpgenerator}
        \li Compiles Qt Help Project (\c{.qhp}) files into compressed \c{.qch}
            archives consumable by Qt Assistant and the Qt help framework.
    \endtable

*/
